# Editor (`wiimaker edit`)

Before deep work, read `MEMORY/durable/editor.md`. After lasting discoveries, update that file.

eframe/egui shell over the same scene files agents edit via CLI. Launch: `cargo run -p wiimaker-editor -- <game>` (or `wiimaker edit`).

## Layout (keep Unity-shaped)

```
Scene viewport | Hierarchy | Inspector
---------------+-----------+----------
Project: file explorer (assets / scenes / game.toml)
```

- Hierarchy: tree / create / rename / delete / select / drag-drop reparent
- Inspector: entity (Local Transform + parent + components) **or** selected project file (meta + actions)
- Viewport: live `render_world` blit; pick/drag uses world transforms
- Project: browse game files; PNG → Edit Sprites / assign; `.scene.json` → open / set default

## Mutation rule

All edits go through `wiimaker-scene` helpers (`add_entity`, `remove_entity`, `set_entity_parent`, `set_entity_transform` / `set_entity_world_xy`, `add_component_*`, `set_scene_clear`, load/save). Then set `dirty` and `rehydrate()` the preview `World`.

```rust
// ❌ BAD — edit World or invent parallel JSON writes
world.spawn(...);
serde_json::to_writer(...); // bypassing save_scene

// ✅ GOOD
add_entity(&mut self.scene, &name, &MutateOpts { .. })?;
self.dirty = true;
self.rehydrate();
// Save → save_scene(&self.scene_path, &self.scene)
```

## State pattern

`EditorApp` holds: `GameProject`, `Scene`, `scene_path`, `dirty`, `selected`, `World`, `TextureAtlas`, viewport `Framebuffer`. After asset cook/reload, rebuild atlas and rehydrate.

Play shells `wiimaker run` / `cargo run -p <game>` — do not fold egui into the fast play path.

## Out of scope (v0)

Visual scripting, full ECS UI, TEV materials, Wiimote IR picking, editing C/GX bootstrap.

## Visual chrome (1:1 Unity 6 dark)

Match these crops — not memory, not a light skin, not extra widgets:

- `MEMORY/durable/unity-chrome/hierarchy.png`
- `MEMORY/durable/unity-chrome/inspector.png`

Rules that fail a review if broken:

1. **Dark Pro only.** Never Unity Personal light grey.
2. **Hierarchy toolbar** is `+` then Search. No per-row Duplicate/Delete buttons; those are right-click / shortcuts. Selection is a full-width blue row, no `>`/`+` name prefixes. (`hierarchy.png`)
3. **Inspector GameObject header** is name (+ Tag). Parenting lives in Hierarchy, not an Unparent button. (`inspector.png`)
4. **Transform** is Position / Rotation / Scale, **one row per property**, X/Y/Z DragValues with axis chips — not sliders stacked per axis. (`inspector.png`)
5. **Add Component** is a wide button under the stack. Component ⋮ menu is Remove Component. (`inspector.png`)
6. Icons are geometric stand-ins. Do not copy Unity’s cube/logo artwork.

If a chrome change disagrees with a crop, the crop wins.
